SecureARC is a high-performance RFC 8617 ARC (Authenticated Received Chain)
milter written in Zig. It integrates with Postfix via the milter protocol
(v6) to validate ARC chains on inbound mail and seal outbound/forwarded
mail with new ARC sets, preserving authentication results across
forwarding hops.

Features:
- ARC chain validation (ARC-Message-Signature and ARC-Seal)
- ARC sealing for forwarded messages (AAR + AMS + AS)
- RSA-SHA256 and Ed25519-SHA256 algorithm support
- Separate verify/seal/both modes per listener
- Thread-per-core worker pool with kqueue I/O multiplexing
- Authentication-Results header generation (RFC 8601)
